  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Nastya decides to leave the restaurant party early because she is feeling bored. Kostya rushes after her to stop her from leaving, as he has something very important to tell her.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Настя, подожди!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Пока.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "О, уже уходишь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Ага. Как-то здесь невесело.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не уходи так быстро.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "У меня много дел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я хочу поговорить с тобой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "О чем ты хочешь поговорить?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это очень важно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Говори быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Подойди поближе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Я слушаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не могу молчать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, выслушай меня.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around Leaving the Party line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Пока.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Bye.' A crisp, everyday conversational reply meaning 'bye' that you will hear constantly in Russian dialogue.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "О, уже уходишь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, you are leaving already?' Kostya turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'already', followed by 'are leaving'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Ага. Как-то здесь невесело.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yeah. It is kind of a downer here.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'yeah' directly with 'somehow', combining 'yeah' with 'somehow' and 'here'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, выслушай меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Please, hear me out.' Kostya leads with the direct command form meaning 'hear out' to make the point directly in conversation. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
